ete Applied Mathematics"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop (XGI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" allows both).","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedHypergraph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph"}}}